{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-e2-reviewer-fable-26","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:c38b4b95d2ca5a382f67","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow aggregates each module's repeated daily logs before any inferential procedure: collapse_to_modules reduces the six rows per planter to one record containing a screened mean, an open mean, and their contrast, yielding exactly one analysed row per independent unit (module_id).","observed_value":"14 module-level records built from per-module fmean of screened days and open days","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":37,"end_line":44,"quoted_text":"def collapse_to_modules(logs):\n    \"\"\"Reduce each module's repeated logging days to one analysed row.\"\"\"\n    records = []\n    for unit in sorted({unit for unit, _state in logs}):\n        screened_days = logs[(unit, SCREENED)]\n        open_days = logs[(unit, OPEN_TOP)]\n        screened_mean = fmean(screened_days)\n        open_mean = fmean(open_days)"}]},{"description":"The paired t-test is run on the module-level aggregates, not on the raw session rows: the lists passed to scipy.stats.ttest_rel are built from `records` (one element per module), so the row-independent procedure receives 14 paired values, one per independent unit.","observed_value":"stats.ttest_rel applied to 14 per-module screened means vs 14 per-module open means","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":63,"end_line":70,"quoted_text":"def build_report(records, n_sessions):\n    screened = [record[\"screened\"] for record in records]\n    open_top = [record[\"open\"] for record in records]\n    contrasts = [record[\"contrast\"] for record in records]\n    n_modules = len(records)\n    df = n_modules - 1\n\n    outcome = stats.ttest_rel(screened, open_top)"}]},{"description":"The reported statistic carries the module-level sample size: t(13) with n = 14 modules, not t(83) or n = 84. Recomputing t from the reported contrast summary, -0.350 / (0.210 / sqrt(14)) = -6.24, matches the reported -6.22 within rounding of the tabled summary values, confirming the test was computed on the 14 module contrasts.","observed_value":"t(13) = -6.22, n = 14 modules; recomputed t ≈ -6.24 from mean contrast -0.350, SD 0.210","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":48,"end_line":49,"quoted_text":"- Mean contrast: -0.350 mm/day (SD 0.210, n = 14 modules)\n- Paired t-test: t(13) = -6.22, p < 0.001"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":51,"end_line":51,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Averaging each planter's repeated days into one analysed row per module (n = 14 independent modules from 84 session rows), a two-sided paired t-test shows that screened days use less water than open days: mean contrast -0.350 mm/day (SD 0.210), t(13) = -6.22, p < 0.001."}]},{"description":"The report's stated analysis explicitly treats the 14 modules as the units and disclaims the 84 daily logs as replication, matching what the code does; module-level means in the report's table check out against the raw CSV (e.g., P01 screened days 4.46, 4.24, 4.47 give mean 4.390 and open days 4.74, 4.89, 4.95 give mean 4.860, as tabled).","observed_value":"report table P01: screened 4.390, open 4.860, contrast -0.470; verified against raw rows","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":14,"end_line":19,"quoted_text":"The 84 session rows are repeated measurements rather than 84 independent\nobservations: six of them belong to each planter. Every module's three\nscreened days and three open days were therefore averaged first, and the\nmodule-level contrast (screened mean minus open mean) was what entered the\ntest. That leaves exactly one analysed row per planter module, so the units\nin the reported comparison are the 14 modules, not the 84 daily logs."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":29,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"| P01 | 6 | 4.390 | 4.860 | -0.470 |"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"P01,open,1,2025-07-08,28.9,4.74\nP01,screened,1,2025-07-09,30.4,4.46\nP01,open,2,2025-07-10,31.2,4.89\nP01,screened,2,2025-07-11,30.1,4.24\nP01,open,3,2025-07-12,28.4,4.95\nP01,screened,3,2025-07-13,29.6,4.47"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The raw input is long-format with each independent unit (module_id) appearing six times, so the preconditions for the issue class exist in the data: feeding these rows directly into a row-independent test would repeat each unit six times. This is the strongest prima facie case for the issue, but it is resolved because the workflow aggregates to one row per module before testing.","observed_value":"84 data rows; each module_id appears 6 times (3 screened, 3 open)","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"Because every planter appears six times, the file is in long format and the\nrows are repeated measurements of the same fourteen planters, not eighty-four\nindependent observations."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":16,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: module_id"}]},{"description":"read_sessions ingests all 84 daily rows and the raw daily values are retained in per-(module, state) lists, so raw session-level data does flow into the analysis; however, downstream these lists are only used to compute per-module means and the session count, never as direct inputs to the t-test.","observed_value":"raw daily et_mm_day values appended to logs[(module_id, screen_state)] lists","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":30,"end_line":34,"quoted_text":"    logs = defaultdict(list)\n    with path.open(newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n        for row in csv.DictReader(handle):\n            logs[(row[UNIT_COL], row[STATE_COL])].append(float(row[RESPONSE_COL]))\n    return logs"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to demonstrate the issue by tracing every path from the 84 raw session rows to the inferential procedure. The only call to a statistical test is stats.ttest_rel(screened, open_top) in build_report, and both arguments are list comprehensions over `records`, the output of collapse_to_modules, which contains exactly one element per distinct module_id (14 elements). The raw per-day lists from read_sessions are consumed only by fmean within collapse_to_modules and by the n_sessions row count; no test statistic touches them directly. I also checked the reported output for signatures of pseudoreplication: degrees of freedom are 13 (consistent with n = 14 modules, not 83 for 84 rows), and recomputing t from the 14 tabled contrasts (mean -0.350, SD 0.210) yields about -6.24, matching the reported -6.22, whereas a test on 84 rows would produce a different df and a substantially different statistic. I further spot-verified the module-level means in the report table against the raw CSV (P01 and others) and confirmed the aggregation is faithful. The attempt to falsify the 'no issue' conclusion failed on every check.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}